        "title": "`INVITE_*` gateway events now require `MANAGE_CHANNELS` in every channel or `ADMINISTRATOR` globally",
        "user": {
          "login": "hampuskraft",
          "id": 24176136,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI0MTc2MTM2",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hampuskraft",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "labels": [
          {
            "id": 349418148,
            "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWwzNDk0MTgxNDg=",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/discord-api-docs/labels/bug",
            "name": "bug",
            "color": "ee0701",
            "default": true,
            "description": null
          }
        ],
        "state": "closed",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 3,
        "created_at": "2023-05-04T14:18:15Z",
        "updated_at": "2023-05-04T18:18:02Z",
        "closed_at": "2023-05-04T18:18:01Z",
        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nDespite having the correct intents set, receiving any `INVITE_*` events over the gateway now requires `ADMINISTRATOR` (1 << 3) globally or `MANAGE_CHANNELS` (1 << 4) in every channel it should receive events for. An invite logger bot in a smaller server was functioning just fine until recently. The last known working timestamp is `2023-05-02T12:43:47.638Z`, but seeing as nobody has reported this bug here yet, I'd guess it's a very recent change.\r\n\r\n### Steps to Reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Add a bot to a guild and assign it a role with `MANAGE_GUILD` (1 << 5).\r\n2. Connect to the gateway using the bot token and specify the `GUILD_INVITES` (1 << 6) intent.\r\n3. Create/delete an invite using relevant endpoints and observe how no `INVITE_*` events are received.\r\n4. Assign the role every single permission *but* `ADMINISTRATOR` (1 << 3).\r\n5. Repeat step 3, with the same result.\r\n6. Now, assign `ADMINISTRATOR` (1 << 3), and repeat step 3. This time `INVITE_*` events are received.\r\n7. Remove all permissions but `MANAGE_GUILD` (1 << 5) from the role and create a permission overwrite for the role in the channel(s) in question with `MANAGE_CHANNELS` (1 << 4).\r\n8. Repeat step 3. This time `INVITE_*` events are received for that channel only.\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nEither one of `MANAGE_GUILD` (1 << 5) globally or `MANAGE_CHANNELS` (1 << 4) per channel should be required, which remains the check for the `GET /guilds/<guild_id>/invites` endpoint (not filtered by `MANAGE_CHANNELS` permission overwrites in the channels).\r\n\r\n### Current Behavior\r\n\r\n`ADMINISTRATOR` (1 << 3) is now required to receive such events globally, or `MANAGE_CHANNELS` (1 << 4) in every channel it should receive events for.\r\n\r\n### Screenshots/Videos\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/24176136/236239307-67b7eeb9-18e0-4e3a-8200-6dbb9d704488.mp4\r\n\r\n### Client and System Information\r\n\r\nN/A, directly using the latest stable API & gateway.",
