        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 0,
        "created_at": "2023-05-02T19:57:07Z",
        "updated_at": "2023-05-03T18:28:43Z",
        "closed_at": null,
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nIf you assign a role to a prompt in Onboarding, then delete the role, the prompt is not changed and when users choose it in Onboarding, the role id will be added to their member object even though the role doesn't exist anymore.\r\n\r\nThis can break the functionality of bots and API libraries if they try to fetch role information of a role that doesn't exist.\r\n\r\n### Steps to Reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Create a role\r\n2. Enable Onboarding\r\n3. Assign the role for a prompt in Onboarding\r\n4. Delete the role\r\n5. From another account, join the server and choose the prompt during Onboarding\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nEither the API should stop the role from being deleted if used in Onboarding, or not add the role ID to the member's object.\r\n\r\n### Current Behavior\r\n\r\nThe role ID is added to the member's `role` property in the user object and its returned when the member is fetched but the role doesn't exist anymore.\r\n\r\n### Screenshots/Videos\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Client and System Information\r\n\r\nStable 194296 (68c6883) Windows 10 64-Bit",
